{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JFXSvpvXfyd8fvB28zKsCN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## foreman-handoff-dashboard â€” grounded bullet claims\n\n**What it is**\n- The session is a trio handoff (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) producing a single Foreman-ready build artifact: `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`, alongside `STAGE0-FRAMING.md`, `DESCRIPTION.md`, `DASHBOARD.md`, `foreman.config.json`, and `EXECUTION-LOG.md`.\n- North Star: a locally-served, **read-only** web dashboard giving John one morning view of Aurora's nightly fleet â€” results + health-at-a-glance + a visual catalog explorer â€” so he never reads raw JSON/markdown.\n\n**Hard constraints (the locked invariants)**\n- Read-only against `kb/aurora.db` (`file:...?mode=ro` + `PRAGMA query_only=ON` + a write-rejecting guard) and `reports/`; never writes KB/library/reports; never reads `.env`.\n- Bound to `127.0.0.1:5001`. Test command: `python -m pytest tests/ -k dashboard -q`.\n- **Additive only** â€” all new code under `dashboard/` + root launcher `aurora_dashboard.py` + `tests/test_dashboard_*.py`; no edits to existing Aurora modules, no migrations.\n- Architectural boundary: the data layer NEVER imports Flask; the blueprint NEVER imports orchestrator/sweep code â€” so it can later mount as an Anchor tab.\n- Working tree is production: every wave ends clean and committed; tests may only increase, never weaken.\n\n**The six waves (run in series, each depends on the prior)**\n- **W1 â€” scaffold + data layer + serving shell:** `dashboard/` package, proven read-only DB handle, blueprint factory (`create_blueprint`/`create_app`), report-reader skeleton, freshness fingerprint, HTML shell with \"as of\" stamp + fingerprint poll. Proves read-only rejection and embeddability on a bare Flask app.\n- **W2 â€” morning glance panel:** parses `reports/morning/latest_summary.json` + briefing note + latest weekly; `/api/morning`; top-finds cards, productivity/adoption line (always with window + sample_size, never a bare %), cost rollup (MTD), noise headline.\n- **W3 â€” errors/health panel:** run status + `critic_c` degrade flag, noise_audit categories with expandable offending rows, backfill audits, reject tails, path-allowlisted `sweep_log_tail`; `/api/health` + `/api/health/detail`. Signals expand in-page (G3).\n- **W4 â€” \"what was new\" per-sweep browser:** `list_sweep_dates` / `read_sweep` (allowlisted to `reports/<kind>/`); `/api/sweeps` + `/api/sweep/<kind>/<date>`; kindÃ—date selector reached from morning finds-new links.\n- **W5 â€” catalog taxonomy map (G1 v1):** `artifacts` LEFT JOIN `embeddings` grouped by `kind Ã— domain_path` (NULL â†’ \"unclassified\"), mean interest_score, dead-link/stars overlay from `link_health`, `hh_events` usage; D3 sunburst reusing `library/_map.html` idiom with click-to-filter.\n- **W6 â€” polish, embeddability proof, docs:** global aggregate freshness header, audited empty/error states, `DASHBOARD.md` with exact Anchor-tab mount steps, integration test mounting on a second bare Flask app exercising every route, live read-only smoke proving mtimes unchanged, plus a **deferred** note for the force-directed knowledge-graph (not built).\n\n**Named traps the plan explicitly guards against**\n- Read-only-safety trap (write rejection / unchanged mtimes â€” hard constraint #1).\n- Coupling/embeddability trap (blueprint works without any Aurora import â€” PM2).\n- Path-traversal / secret-exposure trap (`../../.env` or absolute paths refused â€” hard constraint #2).\n- Thin-window adoption trap (inherited from the quality build â€” always label window + sample_size).\n\n**Grounding notes**\n- Data contract is grounded in `kb/schema.sql` and the live `reports/` surfaces as of 2026-06-11; cited row counts are dated snapshots that drift, so every query resolves its set by rule.\n- The root launcher mirrors the existing `anchor_server.py` pattern.\n\nOne caveat: I summarized only the member document you anchored (the Implementation Plan). If you want the Stage-0 framing/gap-decisions or execution-log folded in, point me at them and I'll extend."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7083,"cache_read_input_tokens":33548,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7083},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"511e3527-e933-4d89-83c6-8139efed9d91","uuid":"3e338a25-3be5-43fe-842f-1e6d2b345796","request_id":"req_011CcBosPNeixVhTqriZiqpi"}
